    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0232" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 European War, 1939/50: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dooman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-04T21:00:00+09:00">September 4,
                            1939—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 4—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>455. Our 453, September 4, noon,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d201-f1"/> paragraph 2.
                    Following is our translation of Cabinet statement released this evening: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Imperial Government will not become involved in the conflict which
                            has suddenly broken out in Europe, but will devote all its energies
                            toward resolving the China incident.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Peiping. Peiping, please repeat to Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dooman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
